  {
   "title": "Nása and sa may",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "When you answer a question that starts with **násaán** (where is…?), **sa** changes to **nása** to show where a person or thing is: **nása loób** (inside), **nása likurán** (behind). This is the same nása you met in Lesson 25. The sentence *Táyo ay nása pagítan ng lángit at lupà* above is an example."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Sa + may** means *near* or *about*. Use it when you are not quite sure exactly where someone or something is."
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "Sa may + place",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Near a place",
       "chips": [
