  {
   "title": "Coming from a place",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "To say where a person **has been** (where they came from), it is clearer to use **gáling sa**, **mulâ sa** or **búhat sa** than sa alone. All three mean *from*."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "In fact gáling, mulâ and búhat already mean *from* by themselves, so word for word these phrases say *from from*. After the sa phrase comes the name of a place (as in Lesson 25)."
    },
